raye-apps (0.5~beta1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Task Manager: the Performance page no longer blinks at each refresh,
    and the Run new task and confirm sheets are opaque and dim the
    window behind.
  * Run new task opens Raye's own apps for regedit, taskmgr, control and
    cmd, refuses windowed programs as root and says why, and shows what
    a root command printed.
  * Task Manager checks a process again after the password before
    changing its priority, and shows the PID of services with a dash in
    their name.
  * Registry Editor asks for the root password for every system change,
    Undo included, and won't touch files a package ships, keys that make
    root load code, /etc/environment or the login screen's
    GreeterEnvironment.
  * Registry Editor opens .rayereg files and asks before importing them.
  * Calendar writes dates month first in English, keeps a repeating
    event when importing its moved dates, keeps the editor open when
    saving fails, and no longer loses reminders more than a year away.
    Repeat rules it cannot follow show their first date only, and it
    says so.
  * Control Panel's Administrative Tools is now System Tools, and the
    apps speak of root instead of administrator.
  * Screen share pickers start with "remember this choice" switched off.
  * American spelling and plainer wording in Calendar, Control Panel,
    Registry Editor and Task Manager, and the missing French strings.
  * raye-calendar, raye-taskmanager and xdg-desktop-portal-raye depend
    on raye-style; raye-taskmanager recommends kde-cli-tools.
  * Control Panel: the classic items, each with its tasks; category pages
    with the list of categories on the side; breadcrumb; search through
    tasks.
  * Control Panel: disk encryption, firewall, backup and restore, display,
    File Explorer options, credential manager and more; Disk Cleanup,
    Character Map and Remote Desktop Connection in System Tools.
  * Control Panel hides what this PC cannot use, like Wi-Fi without a
    card.

 -- techoraye <190692880+techoraye@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:42:05 +0000

raye-apps (0.3~beta1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Task Manager gets Performance, Startup apps, Users, Details and
    Services pages, apps grouped with their processes, search and
    sorting. System Monitor is no longer needed.
  * New Raye Calendar: dates with reminders, day, week, month and agenda
    views, simple repeats, colours, optional public holidays and .ics
    import and export. Events live in one file on this computer, a
    reminder is a notification with Later and Dismiss, and nothing runs
    between two reminders.
  * New Control Panel, with categories, large and small icons,
    Administrative Tools and search, opening the matching Settings page.
  * New Registry Editor for Raye: settings files, desktop settings and
    system defaults as keys, with backups, undo, export and import, and
    an administrator prompt for system files.

 -- techoraye <190692880+techoraye@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:00:18 +0000

raye-apps (0.2~beta1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Raye Task Manager: a Processes tab with End task and Efficiency mode,
    and readable Status, CPU and Memory columns.
  * A Raye picker for what to share when an app shares the screen.
  * Stock apps get plain names in English and French, and their old name
    still finds them in search.
  * The emoji panel replaces the stock selector, in search too.
  * Packages that installed nothing are gone, and raye-taskmanager no longer
    pulls in ksysguard.

